<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">Condrusi</h1><p class="st-meta">300 BCE – 57 BCE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">One of the Germani Cisrhenani of the Belgian uplands, remembered in the name of the Condroz.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Caesar names the Condrusi with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/eburones">Eburones</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/caeroesi">Caeroesi</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/paemani">Paemani</a> as Germani living west of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a>, and calls them clients of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/treveri">Treveri</a>. They lived south of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meuse">Meuse</a> in the region still called the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/condroz">Condroz</a>, between <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-namur">Namur</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/prince-bishopric-of-liege">Liège</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Nothing is known of their rulers or settlements.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>They joined the Belgic league in 57 BCE. In 53 BCE they asked Caesar to spare them from his war on the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/eburones">Eburones</a>. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> they were absorbed into the civitas of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/tungri">Tungri</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/condrusi.jpg" alt="Condrusi" width="320" height="250"><figcaption>Image: Excursions scolaires · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:R%C3%A9gions_naturelles_de_Belgique.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>300 BCE – 57 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Celtic polytheism</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/belgium">Belgium</a></dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-178&amp;focus=condrusi" aria-label="Condrusi on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4790 408 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Condrusi lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5135 708h0M5304 942h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5110 664h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5110 664h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Belgium. <a href="/atlas?year=-178&amp;focus=condrusi">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

